Azure Storage Redundancy is used to protect data against failures. 
LRS stores 3 copies within the same datacenter and is the cheapest option. 
ZRS stores data across 3 availability zones within the same region, protecting against zone failures. 
GRS replicates data to a secondary Azure region, providing disaster recovery against regional outages. 
GZRS combines ZRS in the primary region with geo-replication to a secondary region, offering the highest level of durability and availability. 
For production critical applications, GZRS is generally preferred, while LRS is suitable for development and testing environments.



